  "body": "**Tier:** T4 (money path, tests only). **Why:** regressions for fix rounds 10 and 11 of the trials stack: a never-billed trial-conflict cancel must void every open invoice first so a racing first payment is never cancelled (Sol B-673-1 narrowed, round 11); a trial-ending notice must not promise a charge on a card removed during its admission (Sol B-672-3), a trial-conflict retry must never cancel a plan that already paid (Sol B-673-1), and a supersession committed while the worker reads Stripe must veto the cancel (Sol B-673-2). **T4 trigger scan:** money (Stripe subscription cancellation, paid-invoice evidence, charge copy). No source, schema, dependency or config change in this PR. **T3 trigger scan:** none (tests only). **Bounded T1:** none. **Canonical builder:** B-TR4-119 (agent 119); round 2 by B-TR5-119 (agent 119); round 3 (shared-rule spec) by B-TR8-120 (agent 120); restack by B-TR9-121 (agent 121). **Parent owner:** #656 via T3 #673 (base `agent115/trials-split-3-checkout-webhook`). **Acceptance evidence:** failing-before and passing-after CI lane runs below. **Promotion triggers:** none (already T4).\n\nSplit piece T4 of the trials stack (T1 #671 -> T2 #672 -> T3 #673 -> T4), opened after 12:33 PDT 10-04, so the 1,500-line ceiling applies: **1,239 changed lines** after round 3 (3 files, tests only; 940 after round 2; 423 at opening). New tests for the round-10 fixes live here because #672 and #673 are grandfathered at the 3,000 ceiling (#672 2,968, #673 2,947 after round 10). Lands with the stack as one (MERGE_DEPENDENCY_GUIDE rule 11).\n\n`test/b-trials-4-fix-round.spec.ts` (23 tests): real TrialConflictService + real StripeConnectApiService over an intercepted fetch; real TrialNoticeService over the constraint-aware fakes.\n- B-673-1: past_due and unpaid after a paid first invoice (supersede, no DELETE, one billed alert); a zero-decimal currency charge and a credit-balance payment count as billed; never billed (only the $0 trial invoice, complete page) cancels once; the list is one bounded page (`subscription`, `status=paid`, `limit=100`); an incomplete page, a malformed list, an invoice without `amount_paid`, a 503 and a 404 on the list each retry as `history_unknown` with no DELETE; repeated unknown history alerts support once; `canceled` reads no invoices.\n- B-673-2: a supersession, a subscription-deleted webhook or a lease takeover committed during the GET, and a supersession during the paid-invoice read, each return `stale` with no DELETE; an unchanged trial cancels once.\n- Round 2, `test/b-trials-5-fix-round.spec.ts` (34 tests): Sol's AUD-SOL-T23D-119 payment-race probe with its exact inputs (past_due and unpaid: no DELETE, stays owed, next webhook supersedes); never-billed control (open list, paid list, confirmed void, one DELETE, in that order); payment wins the void (retry, then superseded, one alert); open list read before the paid list; six unconfirmed void answers and six unknown open lists (no DELETE); lease budget; cancel-failing alert once; trialing control; supersession, deletion and lease takeover during the void and during the open read (stale, no DELETE); C-673-7 malformed amounts. `b-trials-4-fix-round.spec.ts` routes the open list and the void (+4/-1).\n- Round 3, `test/b-trials-8-shared-rule.spec.ts` (8 tests, B-TR8-120): ONE SHARED TRIAL RULE. Capability registration and offer; a native trial blocks the next checkout (0 trial days) and the offer (`already_used`); both start orders (winner gets access, loser no access + owed conflict, redelivery stays vetoed); loser first seen active (paid plan, superseded, no trial recorded); loser first seen past_due (owed); loser ended after its trial (never counted, conflict cancelled); a trial first seen at its end still claims the trial. Each test asserts the ledger and `trial_started_at` agree.\n- B-672-3: a customer card removed or added during the final purchase read is reported truthfully on push and on email; every admission reads both authorities in one REPEATABLE READ transaction.\n\n| Round | Head | Failing-before | Passing-after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 (opening, B-TR4-119) | `a3f01163` | [run 37230366374](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37230366374) on T3 `5fdb5f5c`: 20 behavioural failures, 3 controls green | [run 37231152495](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37231152495) at T4 `a3f01163`: 23/23, plus every b-trials spec and every prior lens probe (280/291; the 11 reds are the ruled ones, see OPENING comment) |\n| 2 (B-TR5-119) | `3d95f96e` | [run 37236196278](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37236196278) on T3 `904b9642`: 36 assertion failures, 27 green (b-trials-4 and controls) | [run 37237173197](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37237173197): tsc + every b-trials spec 236/236; probes [run 37237162635](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37237162635) 70/75 (the 5 reds are the ruled Cs) |\n| 3 (B-TR8-120) | `9567f8bd` | [run 37356010489](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37356010489): shared-rule spec on main's side of the #673 merge: 8/8 red | [run 37355951522](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-backend/actions/runs/37355951522): 8/8 + tsc; PR CI at `9567f8bd` |\n| restack (B-TR9-121) | `87aaf126` | — (merge-only: T3 `91d0adcb`, no conflicts, #706 diff byte-identical) | PR CI at `87aaf126` |\n\n",
